# Docs & Code Generation

## Never edit `docs/` manually

Files under `docs/` are generated by `tfplugindocs`. Edit schema `MarkdownDescription` fields and `examples/` instead, then regenerate.

## Examples layout

Mirror Terraform registry conventions:

```
examples/
  provider/provider.tf
  resources/<resource_type>/resource.tf
  data-sources/<data_source_type>/data-source.tf
```

Resource type names must match the provider metadata (e.g. `kilhog_resource`).

## Regenerate

```bash
make generate   # runs tools/go generate: copywrite headers, terraform fmt, tfplugindocs
```

CI fails if `make generate` produces uncommitted changes.

## Provider name in generation

The `-provider-name` flag in `tools/tools.go` is set to `kilhog`.

## Terraform examples

- Run `terraform fmt` on examples (included in `make generate`).
- Keep examples minimal but runnable; they become registry documentation.

## CHANGELOG

Update `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` when adding user-visible features or fixes.
